B.cI2=new A.p("settingsAction",B.X,"Opt-in: {fn, args?, label?} \u2014 a gear affordance shown next to a selected FOLDER's detail header, fired with that row's id (like menuActions, but a single, separate surface for FEATURE settings \u2014 e.g. sharing/members \u2014 kept distinct from the row \u22ee menu's quick actions and from the attributes/edit-details form's data fields).",B.f,null)
B.cHT=new A.p("rootDashboard",B.V,'Two-level rail: the synthetic root ("Projects", nothing selected) gets a COMPUTED cross-project progress dashboard as its detail \u2014 overall done/active/queued rollup plus one row per top-level project \u2014 built from the existing showProgress rollup cache. The root stays synthetic: no new record, no reparenting.',B.f,null)
B.cVN=new A.p("filterable",B.V,"Opt-in per-column filtering of the TASKS/children column (the two-level rail's column 2, and the narrow children-directory list) via the unified Add-filter engine \u2014 mirrors agenda/tree/cards/report's own \"filterable\" opt-in (AddFilterBar<Record> + applyColFilters). Off (default) renders exactly as before. Session-scoped state only; the pinned strip and the projects (column-1/root) list are never filtered.",B.f,null)
B.cKC=new A.p("followSelection",B.V,"Two-way sync with `board.settings['sel:<table>']`: an external write (e.g. a notepad's resolved [[Wiki Link]] tap) selects + reveals that row here; picking a row here publishes back to the same setting. Off by default (no behavior change).",B.f,null)
