B.cPX=new A.p("linkFromTitleColumn",B.t,'linksTable column that also receives the FROM note\'s own title (default "fromTitle") \u2014 kept in sync on every wiki-link sync pass and on rename of the source note. Lets a backlinks view label each row with the source without a join.',B.f,null)
B.cUh=new A.p("onLinkTap",B.X,"Opt-in action spec { fn, args } fired when a plain Markdown `[label](target)` link (NOT a `[[Title]]` wiki-link, which uses linksTable instead) is tapped in Preview. `target` (the link's raw url/title text) substitutes any literal \"$value\" in args, same as textinput's action. Unset (default) \u2192 the link renders styled but inert, unchanged from before this prop existed.",B.f,null)
B.cKn=new A.p("lazyBlocks",B.V,"Opt-in LAZY read view: builds only on-screen Markdown blocks (ListView.builder) instead of the default eager build-everything-up-front view. For a genuinely long document (e.g. a full encyclopedia article) this is the fix for visible scroll lag. No effect when `readOnly`'s shrinkWrap (inline preview) applies. Off by default \u2014 zero behavior change for existing callers.",B.f,null)
B.cJh=new A.p("jumpToSectionSetting",B.D,'Opt-in "jump to section" (only acts when lazyBlocks is also true): names a board-settings key. When that setting\'s value changes to "<anything>::<heading text>" (the leading part just needs to change to force a re-jump on a repeated tap of the same section \u2014 e.g. a timestamp), the read view animate-scrolls to the first #/##/### heading block matching the text (trimmed, case-insensitive) at an ESTIMATED position \u2014 not pixel-exact.',B.f,null)
B.cFG=new A.p("findEnabledSetting",B.D,'Opt-in "Find in article" (only acts when lazyBlocks is also true): names a board-settings key an external affordance (e.g. a \u22ee "Find in article" action) toggles true/false to open/close an inline search bar rendered above the article. The typed query, per-occurrence match highlighting, match-count feedback ("N of M"), next/prev stepping and scroll-to-match are all self-contained in this widget \u2014 no other prop or host wiring is needed. Plain case-insensitive substring matching only, no regex, no cross-block spans. Unset (default) \u2192 zero behavior change.',B.f,null)
B.cFa=new A.p("serifH1",B.V,"Opt-in encyclopedia-style DISPLAY TITLE: renders a top-level `# ` Markdown heading in a serif font stack (Georgia / Times New Roman / Noto Serif / generic serif fallback \u2014 no new font asset bundled, so this always renders with whatever serif face the platform already has) instead of the body sans-serif, at a larger display size. Applies to every `# ` heading in the document (in practice just the one at the very top \u2014 see `document`) in BOTH the eager and `lazyBlocks` read-view paths. Off by default: zero behavior change for every existing caller.",B.f,null)
B.cEU=new A.p("imagesTable",B.at,"Enables `local:<id>` resolution for a standalone `![alt](src)` image block (and gives inline `![alt](src)` mid-paragraph a real target to resolve, though inline never promotes to a block): the id looks up a row in this table, whose imageSrcColumn holds a base64 payload rendered via the engine's existing local-bytes image path (same as `record`'s image preview) \u2014 never fetched. An http(s) src, or a `local:<id>` that doesn't resolve, always renders as alt text; this node has no image-fetch code at all. Unset (default) \u2192 zero behavior change.",B.f,null)
B.cGn=new A.p("imageSrcColumn",B.t,'Column on imagesTable holding the base64 image payload (default "b64").',B.f,null)
