B.cTg=new A.p("width",B.ae,"Optional fixed width; omit to fill the available width.",B.f,null)
B.cS8=new A.p("presetScope",B.X,"priorun-0802 unit2: `{table, column, value}` \u2014 directly calls BoardState.setScope(table, column, value) on the CHILD board so any scopeColumn-aware node inside it (e.g. bubl's `scopeColumn`) filters by that column, with no scopeTargets declaration needed. Distinct from `scope` above (opens on one specific row via the child's OWN declared scopeTargets). `value` supports the same live-token convention every filter-shaped prop uses ($rowId = this embed own injected row, $selected:<table> = the host board live selection, $playerId, or a literal). FAIL-CLOSED: a configured-but-unresolved token (nothing selected yet) sets the scope to a sentinel matching no real row \u2014 never falls back to unscoped \u2014 unless `scopeOptional: true` is also set. Absent = no setScope call at all (unchanged default).",B.f,null)
B.cJJ=new A.p("scopeOptional",B.V,'Pairs with `presetScope` only. Default false keeps presetScope fail-closed (unresolved token -> sentinel, empty scoped set). Set true to instead CLEAR the scope on an unresolved token (full unscoped child) \u2014 for a user-driven selection-chip use where "nothing selected yet" should show everything, not nothing. Mirrors priolanes\' `scopeOptional`.',B.f,null)
